/**
 * The Founding Era, 1754 to 1817: from the colonies to the first four presidents. Dossier topic exhibit.
 *
 * Structure: a timeline whose spine is the four presidencies (Washington, Adams, Jefferson, Madison), with a
 * wing for the years before the Constitution and a closing wing on sources and voices.
 *
 * Research rules followed here:
 *  - every claim has >=1 source and an honest confidence grade; contested/tradition claims carry a note;
 *  - the exhibit is neither hagiography nor a takedown: the founders' ideals, their politics and their slaveholding
 *    are each stated from the record, and the people left out of "We the People" are given rooms of their own;
 *  - every number that historians dispute (enslaved people in 1770, Black soldiers, Black Loyalists, war dead,
 *    Sedition Act prosecutions, post-1808 smuggling) is shown as a range or a loose estimate and graded contested;
 *  - the 1790 and 1810 census counts were read from a U.S. Census Bureau table (see the research notes);
 *  - direct quotation appears only where the exact wording was read in a fetched text:
 *      Avalon Project (Declaration, Royal Proclamation, Treaty of Paris, Northwest Ordinance, Madison's debates, Federalist
 *      10/51/54, Farewell Address, First Inaugural, Sedition Act), the Library of Congress (Jefferson's rough draft),
 *      Wikisource (Dunmore's Proclamation, Constitution, Washington's will, Jefferson's letter to Banneker, Notes on the
 *      State of Virginia), the Massachusetts Historical Society (Abigail and John Adams, 1776), the Lewis and Clark Journals,
 *      Mount Vernon (Washington's letters as printed there) and Monticello (Jefferson to Brissot as printed there);
 *  - this is a topic dossier, and no photographs exist from this era: every image is a period painting, engraving, map or
 *    document, and images that depict violence or the slave trade are gated by minDepth. `characters` holds seven
 *    CharacterBibles (Franklin, Washington, Adams, Jefferson, Madison, Hamilton, Abigail Adams) with `paintedLikeness: true`:
 *    the owner decided these named founders, who have surviving PAINTED portraits, may be shown with faces in the
 *    reconstruction scenes when the references are those portraits (see foundingScenes.ts); nobody else is given a face;
 *  - the evidence behind each source is recorded in docs/dossier/founding-research-notes.md.
 */
